# The zipped copy of training/ that seeded this repo.
chatMCD-training.zip

# The corpus is NOT redistributed: it is the full text of Marc's thesis, papers
# and patents, and it stays under its original copyright. See LICENSE > SCOPE.
# The pipeline that builds it does ship: build_jsonl.py, fetch_sources.py,
# README.md and system_prompt.md are deliberately not excluded here.
training/corpus/
training/qa/
training/mlx/

# Python 3.12 venv holding gradio, for space/test_api_contract.py only.
# The project venv is 3.14 and gradio pydantic pin has no wheel for it.
.venv-gradio/

# Superseded working material, kept locally only. `trash/` is 120 files of the
# same corpus that is excluded above -- an old full copy of training/, the PDF
# text of papers and theses, academic transcripts, and the Elora provisional
# patent. None of it is redistributable and some of it is commercially
# sensitive. It is one line here or an unrecoverable public commit; git history
# keeps a blob reachable by SHA even after a force-push.
trash/
Claude outputs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- personal data
# The repo ships the machinery, not Marc's personal information. These carry
# private facts rather than code:
#   questions.yaml  asserts private biographical facts as expected answers
#   reports/        78 full answer transcripts that repeat them
#   system_prompt   carries a rule about a private contact detail
#   training/README describes the private source documents behind the corpus
eval/questions.yaml
eval/QUESTIONS_SHA
eval/reports/
training/system_prompt.md
space/system_prompt.md
training/README.md

# The original build plan: it specifies the fine-tuning route that measurement
# later rejected, so publishing it would document a path this project does not take.
chatmcd-build-plan.md

train/bakeoff_contended_4b.json.bak

# ------------------------------------------------- not part of the working system
# The repo ships what actually runs. These are the LoRA fine-tuning route, which
# measurement rejected in favour of retrieval and which nothing in production uses.
train/
convert/

# A catalogue of what went wrong on the way. Useful notes, but this repo documents
# the working system, not the path to it.
docs/DEPLOYMENT_LESSONS.md

# The training-pipeline scripts belong to the fine-tuning route excluded above.
scripts/finish_round.sh
scripts/publish_model.sh
scripts/watchdog.sh
scripts/check_template_alignment.py
scripts/preflight.sh
scripts/model_card.py
scripts/download_bases.sh
